\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces WER vs.\ overlap ratio for English (left) and Twi (right) at three SIR levels. Both languages show the same degradation pattern: WER increases with overlap ratio and decreases with SIR. At 0\,dB SIR with full overlap, English WER exceeds 100\%.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:baseline-wer}{{2}{4}{WER vs.\ overlap ratio for English (left) and Twi (right) at three SIR levels. Both languages show the same degradation pattern: WER increases with overlap ratio and decreases with SIR. At 0\,dB SIR with full overlap, English WER exceeds 100\%}{figure.2}{}}
